        "summary": "Failed: The hosted page likely has a bug in the controlled state for the Ghana residence selector: the chip removal UI is visible, but the removal event either does not fire or does not mutate the selected-country state, so Ghana remains as the stored value and is rendered again after the attempted clear. This can happen if the chip is only visually hidden, if the component is using stale props/local state, or if the deployment is serving an outdated build where the remove handler is missing or… Target: environment github-pr-1 (https://github.com/samscript18/GrantPath/pull/1).",
        "apiOutput": null,
        "trace": null,
        "analysis": {
          "rootCauseHypothesis": "The hosted page likely has a bug in the controlled state for the Ghana residence selector: the chip removal UI is visible, but the removal event either does not fire or does not mutate the selected-country state, so Ghana remains as the stored value and is rendered again after the attempted clear. This can happen if the chip is only visually hidden, if the component is using stale props/local state, or if the deployment is serving an outdated build where the remove handler is missing or broken. Underlying error: TEST FAILURE\n\nThe Ghana residence could not be cleared. The selected Ghana chip and residence value remained visible after removal was attempted.\n\nObservations:\n- The “Your world” profile stage showed Ghana in the country-of-residence field.\n- The Ghana selection chip remained visible after two removal attempts.",
          "recommendedFixTarget": {
            "kind": "unknown",
            "reference": null,
            "rationale": "Inspect the country-of-residence multi-select/remove-chip implementation on the hosted build. The failure suggests the chip removal handler is not updating the underlying form state and/or the rendered value after clicking remove. Fix by wiring the clear/remove action to the same controlled state used by the field, ensuring the selected country is actually deleted from state, the input value is reset, and the chip is conditionally re-rendered from that updated state. Also verify there is no CSS overlay or disabled pointer behavior preventing the click from reaching the handler, and confirm the deployed bundle matches the latest source with the removal logic included."
          },
          "failureKind": "unknown",
          "snapshotId": "snap_43a3599227e7065f"
        }
